# TME reverse proxy — Caddy (behind Cloudflare, proxied / orange cloud)
# =============================================================================
# Runs on the HOST (not in Docker Compose). Caddy terminates TLS and forwards to
# the app containers, which publish on 127.0.0.1:${APP_PORT} only
# (see docker-compose.prod.yml: "127.0.0.1:${APP_PORT}:8000").
#
# Request path (izhex.com is proxied through Cloudflare — orange cloud):
#   Telegram -> Cloudflare edge (TLS) -> server: Caddy (TLS) -> 127.0.0.1:${APP_PORT}
#     tme-test.izhex.com -> 127.0.0.1:8081  (tme-test, APP_PORT=8081)
#     tme.izhex.com      -> 127.0.0.1:8080  (tme-prod, APP_PORT=8080)
#
# Because Cloudflare's proxy intercepts the ACME challenge, Caddy can't use
# Let's Encrypt here. We use a Cloudflare ORIGIN CERTIFICATE instead and set
# Cloudflare's SSL/TLS mode to "Full (strict)".
#
# Setup:
#   1. Cloudflare -> SSL/TLS -> Origin Server -> Create Certificate
#      (hostnames: izhex.com, *.izhex.com). Save on the server:
#        sudo install -d -m 755 /etc/caddy/certs
#        sudo tee /etc/caddy/certs/izhex.pem >/dev/null   # paste the certificate
#        sudo tee /etc/caddy/certs/izhex.key >/dev/null   # paste the private key
#        sudo chmod 600 /etc/caddy/certs/izhex.key
#   2. Cloudflare -> SSL/TLS -> Overview -> Full (strict).
#   3. sudo cp deploy/Caddyfile /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#      sudo caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#      sudo systemctl reload caddy
#   4. Open port 443 to Cloudflare. Port 80 is NOT required (no ACME); turn on
#      Cloudflare "Always Use HTTPS" to redirect http->https at the edge.
#
# WEBHOOK_BASE_URL (GitHub Environment Variable) must equal each hostname below,
# e.g. https://tme-test.izhex.com  —  the app appends /webhook/{token}.
#
# NOTE: APP_PORTs below must match the APP_PORT you set per environment. The
# defaults (8081 test / 8080 prod) come from docker-compose.prod.yml.
# =============================================================================

# One Cloudflare Origin Certificate covers izhex.com and *.izhex.com, so the
# same cert/key pair serves both site blocks.
(cf_origin_tls) {
	tls /etc/caddy/certs/izhex.pem /etc/caddy/certs/izhex.key
}

# --- TEST -------------------------------------------------------------------
tme-test.izhex.com {
	import cf_origin_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8081
}

# --- PRODUCTION -------------------------------------------------------------
tme.izhex.com {
	import cf_origin_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
